id: pm-gh1624
title: "GH-1624: define typed Unicode handling for extension output across JSON and TOON"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1624 describes an unpaired UTF-16 surrogate from extension output causing an untyped TOON TypeError while JSON succeeds. Reproduce through the public host command boundary, then define consistent field-aware refusal or explicitly documented normalization and a reusable SDK primitive. This concerns already-malformed external output, distinct from completed persisted-input validation and valid-pair compaction fixes."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-29T14:47:42.900Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T23:35:28.096Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-29T23:35:27.319Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T23:35:27.319Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce nested values and object keys through the actual extension host on Node and Bun; Preserve valid astral pairs and input immutability; Publish the SDK contract and JSON/TOON parity with pre-fix negative controls
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Add reusable SDK Unicode validation and repair helpers; render one validated custom-serialization snapshot consistently through native JSON and TOON, with printable field diagnostics and preserved valid data."
expected_result: "Malformed UTF-16 values and keys receive actionable usage refusals across formats; valid Unicode, caller data and the actual serialized snapshot remain intact on Node and Bun."
actual_result: "Latest linked receipt test-local-mvu696dm-gpjkq5 passes 12 tests; the original host and newer serializer controls fail before their fixes. Clean installed packed-SDK probes pass on Node and Bun, including cross-entrypoint refusal recognition; TypeScript and focused ESLint pass."
